# Python
pipeline/.venv/
pipeline/**/__pycache__/
pipeline/*.egg-info/
pipeline/build/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Cached indexes, contextual prefixes, and extractions. Expensive to regenerate,
# but derived data — rebuildable with --rebuild-index.
pipeline/.index-cache/

# Precomputed results.
#
# These are the deployed site's entire data source, so it is tempting to commit
# them. They are ignored instead, because the only results that exist today are
# synthetic fixtures and a repository whose first commit contains invented
# measurements is worse than one that contains none. results/README.md explains
# how to populate the directory.
#
# Revisit this once a real run exists: committed results are what make the
# deployed site instant and free to visit, and at that point they should be
# tracked deliberately, in a commit that says so.
results/*.json

# Node
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
web/next-env.d.ts
web/.vercel/
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Local env. Both keys live here; nothing in the repo reads a key from anywhere
# else, and no key should ever reach a committed file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
